      "gap": 18,
      "padding": 24,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "RBKif",
          "name": "t",
          "fill": "$text-primary",
          "content": "Agent asleep · put to sleep after 30 minutes without a turn, and how it wakes",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Ao9f3",
          "name": "intro",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1100,
          "content": "An agent with no turn for 30 minutes is put to sleep: Tars ends its CLI, which gives its memory back, and keeps its conversation. It reads asleep, a word in the idle ink after a hollow square, the mark of an agent no CLI holds. One line says since when, where an error gives its reason: in place of the task on its card, of the branch in its pane's header, of the path in its window. A message, a dispatch, a chat, its wake button or a key typed into its terminal wakes it: Tars starts its CLI again on that same conversation, in about a second, and it reads waking until the CLI is up. An orchestrator never sleeps. Asleep is not stopped: a stopped agent was ended on purpose and says by whom and why; a message starts it again too, and the restart notes whose stop it ended.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
