    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "WxqAL",
      "x": 7700,
      "y": 2000,
      "name": "Usage · cost per task",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "dark"
      },
      "width": 1440,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 14,
      "padding": 24,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Deoqz",
          "name": "t",
          "fill": "$text-primary",
          "content": "Usage · cost per task: what each task cost, and the work it handed on",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "A9qwQv",
          "name": "intro",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1100,
          "content": "Under the four charts, across the page, over the page's one timeframe. A task is one piece of work in one agent: it starts at the first turn after a rest, typed in its window or handed to it by another agent, Tars, a chat or a run over ACP, and ends at its next rest. Its own cost is what its replies cost, read from its transcripts at the page's prices; its total adds every task it handed on, down the line, and says partial when one of them is not counted. A CLI that writes no transcript is not counted, never shown as free. The averages are over the tasks listed: the timeframe, then the project and the agent picked. The switch at the head of the list shows the same tasks by agent (Usage · cost per agent), and the page opens on the view last picked.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
