      "theme": {
        "mode": "light"
      },
      "width": 1440,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 14,
      "padding": 24,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "TljdJ",
          "name": "t",
          "fill": "$text-primary",
          "content": "Permission asked of Tars · allow it, deny it with a reason, or send it to the terminal",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "BOyxs",
          "name": "intro",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1100,
          "content": "A Claude agent that runs the state mod asks Tars, not its terminal, before a call Claude Code would put to its permission dialog: its terminal shows no dialog, and it reads waiting. The question is where you look instead. A line under its panel's header says what it asks, the tool and what the call acts on, the command, the file, the address or the search; never a file's content, which Tars is not sent. Its window says it in full, at the top of the terminal column, and its card in place of the task. allow runs the call; deny refuses it, with a reason the agent reads if you give one; ask in terminal puts it to the terminal's dialog, as before the mod. Nothing is typed into the terminal.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
