        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "hxf1v",
          "name": "Parti pris",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "tBilX",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "PARTI PRIS",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "EtYUc",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A project keeps its team: the orchestrator and its agents. You open several chats in a project, each a conversation with the orchestrator on one topic, all served by the same team, several at once. The sidebar becomes the chats, as T3 Code's sidebar is its threads, and the rest of Tars sits behind More at its foot.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "H5hUgz",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Above the chats, a fixed first entry, Tars, all projects: the super orchestrator, whose space is the current Chat page. It sees every project, messages each project's orchestrator and hears from them. It stays as it is, and the chats are added beside it.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "ADRf0",
          "name": "Shell · chats · project page",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "pW5jG",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "SHELL · CHATS · PROJECT PAGE",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "GWpLe",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The sidebar. Main menu: Chat and Projects, then Dashboard, Kanban and Schedules, kept until the chats work well. New chat. Tars, all projects, which the project filter never hides and which opens the Chat page unchanged (drawn in chat-redesign-a.pen as Chat · chats · Tars, all projects). The chat list: the project filter, set to tars here; how many chats work, of the most this Mac runs at once (2 of 3 working); Pinned, Active and Working; Snoozed and Settled folded with their counts.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "fAuR1",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Each row: its title; its project and number (tars #3), fixed in its project, #1 being Main, the number Telegram names a chat by; its state: working, waiting on you (its orchestrator asks a permission), unread (the title in bold too) or asleep. More, at the foot, opens the submenu.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ggcZF",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The page: the project's chats by number, #1 Main first, with their state and last line; its team, with what each agent is on and how many tasks wait in its queue; an entry to its Dashboard terminals; and its room, which opens the Chat page on tars's room.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
